  "goodToKnow": "Unschädlich means harmless: gesundheitlich unschädlich. Unschädlich machen means to neutralise: a criminal, a virus, or a bomb. Unexploded World War II bombs are still found in German cities, often during building work, and the Kampfmittelräumdienst defuses them after evacuating the area. The opposite is schädlich (harmful). Synonym: harmlos."
